    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476-a1">

                <pb facs="0734" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg618"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Circular by the Dean of the Diplomatic Corps in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De Freitas</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Circular No. 187</seg></opener>
                <p>The Dean has the honour to circulate herewith for the information of his
                    Honourable Colleagues, a letter from H. E. The Netherlands Minister<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d476-f1"/> regarding a proposal submitted on January 23,
                    1923, by H. E. the American Minister to the effect that the Representatives of
                    the Treaty Powers in Peking should recommend to their respective Governments the
                    withholding of assistance from China in connection with the construction of
                    naval vessels, arsenals, and dockyards, etc. H. E. The Netherlands Minister has
                    been authorized by his Government to concur in this proposal on condition that
                    it be agreed by other Governments represented in Peking.</p>
                <p>Monsieur de Freitas would be glad to learn whether his Honourable Colleagues have
                    received similar authorization.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
